{
  "name": "building-living-visual",
  "description": "Visual check of living quarters tiers and employee needs display with hunger and fatigue gauges",
  "steps": [
    {
      "command": "new_game seed:42 cash:200000",
      "timeout": 40,
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "new_game seed:42 cash:200000"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "cash": 200000,
          "buildingCount": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "employee hire role:driller",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"employees\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"driller\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"driller\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": ["cash"],
        "equals": {
          "employeeCount": 1
        }
      },
      "description": "Hired ahead of the orders below rather than after them (#556): a build order is queued work now, so the sites need someone on the roster to walk over and build them. Keeping this file’s own hires as the builders — rather than reaching for staffed:true — is what leaves the roster and proficiency counts it asserts where they were."
    },
    {
      "command": "employee hire role:blaster",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"blaster\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"blaster\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": ["cash"],
        "equals": {
          "employeeCount": 2
        }
      },
      "description": "Hired ahead of the orders below rather than after them (#556): a build order is queued work now, so the sites need someone on the roster to walk over and build them. Keeping this file’s own hires as the builders — rather than reaching for staffed:true — is what leaves the roster and proficiency counts it asserts where they were."
    },
    {
      "command": "employee hire role:driver",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"driver\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"driver\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": ["cash"],
        "equals": {
          "employeeCount": 3
        }
      },
      "description": "Hired ahead of the orders below rather than after them (#556): a build order is queued work now, so the sites need someone on the roster to walk over and build them. Keeping this file’s own hires as the builders — rather than reaching for staffed:true — is what leaves the roster and proficiency counts it asserts where they were."
    },
    {
      "command": "build research_center at:30,5",
      "description": "Placed before any research is queued — a placed research_center is a hard prerequisite (#442) to queue a research task at all.",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"build\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-build-panel [data-build-type=\"research_center\"] .bs-build-buy-btn"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        },
        {
          "type": "pickTile",
          "x": 30,
          "z": 5
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "changedBy": {
          "cash": -25000
        },
        "note": "Confirming placement only queues a construction site (#556) — the next step waits for it to actually land before the Queue Research click below depends on hasActiveResearchCenter seeing a real building."
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "wait_until field:buildingCount equals:1 max_ticks:300",
      "description": "Drive the Research Center site to completion (#556).",
      "timeout": 95,
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "waitUntil",
          "field": "buildingCount",
          "equals": 1,
          "maxTicks": 300,
          "timeoutMs": 90000
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "buildingCount": 1,
          "orderedBuildingCount": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "build living_quarters at:5,5 tier:1",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-build-panel [data-build-type=\"living_quarters\"] .bs-build-buy-btn"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        },
        {
          "type": "pickTile",
          "x": 5,
          "z": 5
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "orderedBuildingCount": 1,
          "buildingCount": 1
        },
        "changedBy": {
          "cash": -10000
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "wait_until field:buildingCount equals:2 max_ticks:400",
      "description": "Let the queued construction site(s) be walked to and built out (#556): ordering a building no longer places it, so everything below that needs a standing building waits here first.",
      "timeout": 130,
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "waitUntil",
          "field": "buildingCount",
          "equals": 2,
          "maxTicks": 400,
          "timeoutMs": 120000
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "buildingCount": 2,
          "orderedBuildingCount": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "research queue type:living_quarters tier:2",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "set",
          "selector": "#bs-build-panel [data-build-type=\"living_quarters\"] .bs-build-tier-sel",
          "value": "2"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-build-panel [data-build-type=\"living_quarters\"] .bs-build-research-btn"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-build-panel [data-build-type=\"living_quarters\"] .bs-build-research-btn"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "changedBy": {
          "cash": -5000
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "tick 50",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "tick 50"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup"
    },
    {
      "command": "build living_quarters at:12,5 tier:2",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-build-panel [data-build-type=\"living_quarters\"] .bs-build-buy-btn"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        },
        {
          "type": "pickTile",
          "x": 12,
          "z": 5
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": ["cash"],
        "equals": {
          "orderedBuildingCount": 1,
          "buildingCount": 2
        },
        "note": "cash uses decreased, not equals, because this build follows a tick step — real browser interaction mode keeps ticking on wall-clock time (Finding #12), so the exact post-tick cash value can drift"
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "wait_until field:buildingCount equals:3 max_ticks:400",
      "description": "Let the queued construction site(s) be walked to and built out (#556): ordering a building no longer places it, so everything below that needs a standing building waits here first.",
      "timeout": 130,
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "waitUntil",
          "field": "buildingCount",
          "equals": 3,
          "maxTicks": 400,
          "timeoutMs": 120000
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "buildingCount": 3,
          "orderedBuildingCount": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "research queue type:living_quarters tier:3",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "set",
          "selector": "#bs-build-panel [data-build-type=\"living_quarters\"] .bs-build-tier-sel",
          "value": "3"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-build-panel [data-build-type=\"living_quarters\"] .bs-build-research-btn"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-build-panel [data-build-type=\"living_quarters\"] .bs-build-research-btn"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": ["cash"]
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "tick 50",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "tick 50"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup"
    },
    {
      "command": "build living_quarters at:20,5 tier:3",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-build-panel [data-build-type=\"living_quarters\"] .bs-build-buy-btn"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        },
        {
          "type": "pickTile",
          "x": 20,
          "z": 5
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": ["cash"],
        "equals": {
          "orderedBuildingCount": 1,
          "buildingCount": 3
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "wait_until field:buildingCount equals:4 max_ticks:400",
      "description": "Let the queued construction site(s) be walked to and built out (#556): ordering a building no longer places it, so everything below that needs a standing building waits here first.",
      "timeout": 130,
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "waitUntil",
          "field": "buildingCount",
          "equals": 4,
          "maxTicks": 400,
          "timeoutMs": 120000
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "buildingCount": 4,
          "orderedBuildingCount": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "build list",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "build list"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "employee list",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "employee list"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "needs",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "needs"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "tick 20",
      "description": "#928: widened from tick 5 -- by this point in the file the legacy shift-cycle (hasBunkhouse: a tier-2+ living_quarters is already standing) is active, and #928's single-gauge fatigue model means less proactive need-interruption keeps an employee's ticksWorked accumulating uninterrupted, so one of the three employees is already mid forced-shift-rest (WORK_DURATION_TICKS=6) right as this step starts -- fatigue correctly holds flat while resting (NEED_DRAIN_RATES.fatigue.resting=0, unchanged, #680) rather than draining, so a 5-tick window can catch it between 'still resting' and 'just replenished above its own pre-rest value', making minFatigue non-monotonic for a few ticks. A wider window lets that employee's rest complete, replenish, and resume idle/traveling drain like the rest of the roster, so minFatigue nets downward again (sandbox-measured on seed 42: 86.5 -> 88.5 at +10 ticks (replenished) -> 83.5 at +20).",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "tick 20"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": ["minFatigue"],
        "note": "fatigue accrues even while idle — minFatigue (100=rested) drops within this window with no work assigned, once any in-flight forced rest has completed and replenished"
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "needs",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "needs"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "scores",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "scores"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "state full",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "state full"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    }
  ],
  "shots": [
    {
      "name": "overview",
      "yaw": 0,
      "pitch": 45
    },
    {
      "name": "tier-comparison",
      "yaw": 90,
      "pitch": 15
    },
    {
      "name": "needs-display",
      "yaw": 45,
      "pitch": 30
    },
    {
      "name": "birdseye",
      "yaw": 0,
      "pitch": 80
    }
  ]
}
